<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Internal dataset performance.</span> Average claims (Q1), correct claims (Q2), and useful claims (Q3) per
summary, with correctness/usefulness ratios. We also report uncertainty metrics
<math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\text{CoCoA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mtext>CoCoA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\text{CoCoA}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Q4) and <math id="S4.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\text{ret}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mtext>ret</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\text{ret}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Q5); for each, the value outside parentheses is the uncertainty (↓),
and the value in parentheses is PRR (↑). Arrows in headers indicate the direction of better results.
The LangChain agent does not produce uncertainty metrics (shown as –).</figcaption>
